Using `absl::SkipEmpty()` will skip any genuine empty string arguments in Redis commands (e.g. `SET key ""`), leading to command corruption and wrong database values. Instead, split without `SkipEmpty` and pop the last element (which is always empty due to the trailing `\0`).

```c
      std::string_view read{reinterpret_cast<char*>(ptr->storage.data()), bytes.size()};
      std::vector<std::string_view> split_args = absl::StrSplit(read, '\0');
      if (!split_args.empty() && split_args.back().empty()) {
        split_args.pop_back();
      }
      ptr->args.assign(split_args.begin(), split_args.end());
```

