If `reader_->Read` fails, the function returns without popping the item from `offsets_`. This causes an infinite loop of failing reads on subsequent calls, completely blocking the connection. Mark the connection as closing to safely tear it down.

```c
    auto result = reader_->Read(item.offset, bytes);
    if (!result) {
      LOG(ERROR) << "Could not load item at offset " << item.offset << " of size "
                 << item.total_bytes << " from disk with error: " << result.error().value() << " "
                 << result.error().message();
      cc_->conn_closing = true;
      return;
    }
```

