Declare a destructor for `DiskBackedBackpressureQueue` to clean up the temporary files from `/tmp` when the connection is closed, preventing disk space leaks.

```suggestion
    DiskBackedBackpressureQueue();
    ~DiskBackedBackpressureQueue();
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Implement the destructor to unlink the temporary file from `/tmp` when the connection is closed.

```c
Connection::DiskBackedBackpressureQueue::DiskBackedBackpressureQueue()
    : max_backing_size_(absl::GetFlag(FLAGS_connection_disk_backpressure_file_max_bytes)),
      max_queue_load_size_(absl::GetFlag(FLAGS_connection_disk_backpressure_load_size)),
      watermark_(absl::GetFlag(FLAGS_connection_disk_backpressure_watermark)) {
  id_ = ++unique_id;
}

Connection::DiskBackedBackpressureQueue::~DiskBackedBackpressureQueue() {
  if (init_) {
    writer_.reset();
    reader_.reset();
    std::string backing_name = absl::StrCat("/tmp/backing_", getpid(), "_", id_);
    unlink(backing_name.c_str());
  }
}
```

