![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The current implementation does not handle paths longer than `MAX_PATH`. If `GetFinalPathNameByHandleW` requires a larger buffer, `path_len` will be greater than or equal to `MAX_PATH`, the check for the zombie handle will be skipped, and the infinite loop bug that this PR aims to fix will persist for files with long paths.

To make this fix more robust, you should handle this case by dynamically allocating a larger buffer if the initial stack-allocated buffer is too small.

```c
    WCHAR path_buf_stack[MAX_PATH];
    WCHAR* path_buf = path_buf_stack;
    DWORD path_buf_size = ARRAY_SIZE(path_buf_stack);
    WCHAR* path_buf_heap = NULL;
    DWORD returned_len;

    returned_len = GetFinalPathNameByHandleW(handle->dir_handle,
                                             path_buf,
                                             path_buf_size,
                                             FILE_NAME_NORMALIZED);

    if (returned_len > path_buf_size) {
      path_buf_heap = uv__malloc(returned_len * sizeof(WCHAR));
      if (path_buf_heap == NULL) {
        /* Allocation failed, can't perform check. */
        returned_len = 0;
      } else {
        path_buf = path_buf_heap;
        path_buf_size = returned_len;
        returned_len = GetFinalPathNameByHandleW(handle->dir_handle,
                                                 path_buf,
                                                 path_buf_size,
                                                 FILE_NAME_NORMALIZED);
      }
    }

    if (returned_len > 0 && returned_len < path_buf_size) {
      if (wcsstr(path_buf, L"$Extend\\$Deleted") != NULL) {
        handle->cb(handle, NULL, 0, UV_ENOENT);
        uv__free(path_buf_heap);
        return;
      }
    }

    uv__free(path_buf_heap);
```

![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `#if MICROPY_ENABLE_SOURCE_LINE` block is nested inside the `#if MICROPY_EMIT_NATIVE` block. If `MICROPY_EMIT_NATIVE` is disabled (which is common for many builds), the `source-lines` and `no-source-lines` command-line options will not be recognized, and `mpy-cross` will exit with a usage error when they are used. Moving the `#if MICROPY_ENABLE_SOURCE_LINE` block outside of the `#if MICROPY_EMIT_NATIVE` block resolves this issue.

```c
                #endif
                #if MICROPY_ENABLE_SOURCE_LINE
                } else if (strcmp(argv[a + 1], "source-lines") == 0) {
                    // Allow excluding source lines for debug builds.
                    include_source_lines = true;
                } else if (strcmp(argv[a + 1], "no-source-lines") == 0) {
                    // Allow excluding source lines for debug builds.
                    include_source_lines = false;
                #endif
